 "about_text": "Gallery Side 2 is a contemporary art gallery in Tokyo's Roppongi district, representing a small international roster of artists working across painting, sculpture, installation and photography. Its program brings together Japanese artists such as Jun Fujita, Takeo Hanazawa, Eikei Inamori, Shiko Sato and Masaru Tatsuki with Southeast Asian and Italian figures including Udomsak Krisanamis, Thaiwijit Puengkasemsomboon, Michelangelo Consani and the late Santi Alleruzzo, alongside internationally established names like Rirkrit Tiravanija, Peter McDonald and Jae Yong Rhee. The gallery has staged solo and group exhibitions by these artists over more than two decades, and periodically presents special projects and pop-up events in its space.",
